{"seq":19,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:25:57.001Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"17c45d68bdc7e73dcf175c141ceed191f75a55ae5a9ebb4cfd953cde6c41a089","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Dana, here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes that I can see:\n\n1. #4419: Thea logged it. Gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. Source: North cheat sheet, teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md (undated). The same sheet says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\n2. #PD-4492: Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025. Gatehouse kiosk alerts at Eau Claire: drivers on the 04:00 shift at Doors 14-18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Source: Sunday prep for Ruth, teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the shift cleared. The digest also asks to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\nNotes: the 2025-09-14 North pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon but give no ticket number. The Sept 2025 handoff email from Ilse also cites #4419 but describes it as a Duluth Gate 3 kiosk glitch, which doesn't match the cheat sheet's description. I didn't include #8841 or #PD-8812 because they sit in your own debrief note or on Brackenwater, not in Moss's Quarrendon notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
